# File locking is mandatory

Before changing any repository file, follow the complete locking protocol in `AGENTS.md`.

- Choose one stable, unique `-Owner` for this conversation.
- Run `scripts/file-lock.ps1 list`, then atomically acquire every intended file with `acquire`.
- On conflict, wait or stop. Never edit the locked file and never use `-Force` without explicit user approval.
- Re-read each file after acquiring its lock; do not write from a stale snapshot.
- If additional files become necessary, acquire them before editing.
- Check the diff and release all owned file locks when the change is done or interrupted.
- Acquire the `-Global` lock before any backend/frontend/Tauri/portable build. While another owner holds the global lock, do not edit source or build.

These requirements override the older “touch shared hubs carefully” guidance: careful editing without a lock is not sufficient.
